</subtitle><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><entry><title type="html">Distance to Empty</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/distance-to-empty.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Distance to Empty" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/distance-to-empty</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/distance-to-empty.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Through in-depth interviews with athletes, race organizers and sports scientists, shedding light on the unique challenges involved in tackling 200+ mile races.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Life in Stride</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/life-in-stride.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Life in Stride" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/life-in-stride</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/life-in-stride.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="road" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Goal of the podcast: serve as a safe haven for the “try hard” amateur who loves to balance the demands of family, work and life while building their fastest self.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Out and Back</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/out-and-back.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Out and Back" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.c